Interesting. I'd be in favour of an occasional 'alternate' minetown.
However, the lack of priest would annoy racketeers, and the ghosts
that appear when you enter an abandoned temple would annoy everyone (I
hate those ghosts! Even if you've been to hell and back, and killed
more ghosts, demons and monsters and who knows what than you can
count, you still get "scared to death" and paralysed whenever one
appears in a temple, even with a =oFA. I think this should be removed
from the game, but I digress). Also, bear in mind that a looted
Izchak's means not only no chance of a magic lamp, but no chance of
candles, which are important later in the game. All in all, I'd say
yes to an orc-town but no to a looted minetown, unless adequate
compensation for the above problems can be included somehow . And
while we're at it, how about kobold-town or goblin-town?

Another minetown-tweaking idea might be to make the watch, shopkeepers
and priest of the same race as the town's occupants - it seems odd to
me that the gnomes import a load of humans to do those jobs in their
town. Obviously it could make these NPCs less dangerous, but their
stats could be boosted: Use the "gnome warriors" from slashem for a
tougher gnomish watch, for instance, or kit out the gnomish shopkeeps
with wands of death or badass pets (A la  one-eyed sam) or something.
I suppose they have the watch and the Kops to back them up anyway
(although not in every situation- maybe that could be rectified), so
they don't necessarily need too much more buffing. I believe sporhack
allows NPC priests of varying species - are sporky non-human priests
less tough than human ones, or are they compensated somehow? How does
it affect gameplay?



